## Scanning electron microscopy
ETV2-ECs and ETV2-SPI1-ECs were cultured on coverslips until day 12 of differentiation with VEGFA $(50\mathrm{ng/}$ ml; cat. 100-20, Peprotech). BALB/c LSECs were cultured for $1.5\mathrm{-}2\mathrm{h}$ after isolation, with $(40\mathrm{ng/ml}$ , cat. V4512- 10UG, Sigma Aldrich). Cells were washed thoroughly with PBS to avoid protein and serum remnants. Next, cells were immersed in $500\upmu\mathrm{l}$ PBS and fixed for $10\mathrm{min}$ with $500\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of $5\%$ glutaraldehyde in $66\mathrm{mM}$ cacodylate buffer. The fixative solution was removed and cells maintained overnight at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in $2.5\%$ glutaraldehyde in $66\mathrm{mM}$ cacodylate buffer. Cells were washed with $0.1\ensuremath{\mathrm{M}}$ cacodylate buffer at room temperature and post-fixed for $2\mathrm{h}$ at room temperature with $1\%$ $\mathrm{OsO_{4}}+1.5\%$ ${\mathrm{K}}_{4}{\mathrm{Fe}}({\mathrm{CN}})_{6}$ in $0.1\ensuremath{\mathrm{M}}$ cacodylate buffer. After post-fixation cells were washed with $0.1\ensuremath{\mathrm{M}}$ cacodylate buffer and dehydrated with increasing ethanol concentrations $(30-50-70-90-100-100\%)$ with $5\mathrm{min}$ incubation per concentration. Finally, the samples were critical point dried in a Leica CPD300 critical point dryer and the coverslips with cells mounted on pin stubs with carbon stickers. Cells were observed and imaged in a Zeiss Sigma scanning electron microscope at an accelerating voltage of $5\mathrm{kV}$ . Pore diameters were counted and measured using ImageJ and the EBImage R package.
## FSA-FITC uptake assay
ETV2-ECs and ETV2-SPI1-ECs were cultured until day 12 of differentiation on Matrigel-coated wells in a 24-well plate. BALB/c LSECs were isolated and plated as well on collagen at 200,000 cells per well in a 24-well plate in $0\%$ FBS-DMEM. After $^{\textrm{1h}}$ of LSEC plating, ETV2-ECs, ETV2-SPI1-ECs, and LSECs were supplemented with $10\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ FSA-FITC (prepared as described in ref. 47) and
1:1000 IncuCyte $\textsuperscript{\textregistered}$ NucLight Rapid Red Reagent (cat. 4717, Sartorius). Cells were imaged hourly over a period of $24\mathrm{h}$ using the IncuCyte Cell analysis system (Essen Bioscience). Quantification was performed with the IncuCyte Cell analysis software. This experiment was repeated twice. Statistical differences were assessed by mixed ANOVA.
